+## Skill coverage: the shared Check Question response and the options lessons 1-3 use (lane A, 2026-10-17)
+
+The Skill coverage rule (owner, 2026-10-17) needs every printed item type to be a skill + options. Lane A
+closed the gaps the audit (`lessons/SKILL-COVERAGE-AUDIT-1-5.md`) found in lessons 1-3 and built the one
+response every lesson's Check Question shares.
+
+**"Which is right?" A to D - the universal option `whichRight` (share key 5Z).** One shared module,
+`js/modules/which-right.js`:
+
+- `whichRightAnswers(q, {rightOf})` - the item's right answer and its provider's distinct wrong answers
+  (`wrongAnswers` when the provider lists them, else `wrongAnswer` rotated by seed). `dlCheckQuestion`
+  (print-sheet.js) builds the board's A-D from it, so the board and the online item use ONE set.
+- `applyWhichRight(q, seed)` - the item turned into the choice: `answerType: 'multiple-choice'`, four
+  options (right + three wrong, a seeded order), `ans` the right one, the kit cell `which-right`
+  (`sheet/cells/which-right.js`: the stem, then A-D in ruled boxes with a tick box each; the key ticks
+  the right one). generate-question.js applies it after every other post layer when `opts.whichRight`
+  is true; an item whose provider gives fewer than two wrong answers keeps its own item.
+- The option is in `UNIVERSAL_OPTIONS` (skill-options.js) and is SHOWN only on a skill whose provider
+  names wrong answers (`registerWhichRightFits`).
+
+**How a lesson uses it.** Give the Check Question a ref with the option:
+`checkQuestion: { ref: { categoryId, skillId, opts: { ...the lesson skill's opts, whichRight: true } }, want, correct }`.
+The bridge deals the ref WITHOUT `whichRight` (the board shows the item and its A-D, letters claimed by
+`mistakes[].option`), and `skills.used` records the ref with `whichRight: true` - the online twin of the
+board question. Lessons 1, 2 and 3a do this; lessons 4 onward should too.
+
+**Options lessons 1-3 now set (were lesson-only ref keys).** Defaults change nothing, so every saved code
+deals as before; keys are pinned in skill-option-keys.js.
+
+| Skill | Option (key) | Replaces |
+|---|---|---|
+| composing:number_word_form | `band` 99 (21-99), 999 (101-999, no 1,000); `teens: 'some'` (4O) | `minNum` / `maxNum`, the `pvTeen` hope |
+| placevalue:expand | `teens: 'some'` (4O): one 3-digit number in six ends in a teen | — |
+| placevalue:combine | `story: true` (4N): the parts as a story (groups of 100 and 10, and more) | P5's hand-written `lines` |
+| addition:add_wp_20 | `wpParts: 'bridge'` (3Z), `barFill` (3Y), `wpEquation` (3X), `wpShort` (3W) | `partMin` / `noPart` / `crossTen`, `cellPayload.layout: 'bar'`, `signSlot` (online), `shortQuestion` |
+| multiplication:mult_properties | `task` 3 (a turn story), `minProduct` (3V), `maxProduct` (3U), `minFactor` (5S) | P5's `lines`, `minNum` / `maxNum` / `allTest: 'arrP2'` |
+| multiplication:multiply_three_numbers | NEW skill (build list `mult_three`, 3.OA.B.5 associative): `forms` 0-3, kit cell `three-factors` | lesson 3a's associative clause |
+
+`barFill` / `wpEquation` items answer in several boxes on screen (`q.ans` "13, 8, 5, 13"; the parts in
+either order are accepted) and carry `q.dealAnswer` = the story's answer, which `dlAns`, `itemNumberOf`
+and compose.js `answerOf` read - so the bridge deals and keys them exactly as a one-number story.
+`wpParts: 'bridge'` picks its whole-of-20 stories by the item's SEED (never its page index alone: a page
+place redrawing across seeds is never held to a 20).
+
+**Still lesson-only (page composition, not ranges):** `factorCap`, `edgeLast`, `want` / `allTest` page
+selections (`arrP1`), `fresh`, `itemSpread`, and the P0 / P1 / retrieval floors on earlier-content items
+(audit X3) - noted as `ref` in `skills.used`.
